_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nI ran the three reads you asked for first. The `catalog/` listing showed 8 files. Both `books.py` reads returned only the lines they asked for: lines 1\u20135, then lines 4\u20138. Then I fixed the code. `python3 -m unittest` now runs 16 tests and all pass. I didn't touch the tests.\n\nFixes in `catalog/`:\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` now converts the year to `int`. That fixed both the year check and `age()`.\n- **`factory.py`**: added the missing `Emma` book to `sample_books()`.\n- **`fees.py`**: `late_fee` multiplied by the daily rate where it had been adding it (`+` changed to `*`).\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned `n+1` events. It now returns the last `n` (`[-n:]`).\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3 but the comment and tests say five, so I set it to 5.\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n\nOne extra change you didn't ask for: `recent(0)` now returns an empty list. With `[-n:]` alone, `n=0` would have returned the whole history.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 3, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 23597, "requests_cache_write": 78637, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2148042, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 1582, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial24", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 167, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-17T05:31:53.498837+00:00", "subagent_resu